{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782045841599,"sessionID":"ses_115cdbe95ffeGp0717tT7zELj9","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b266350c60cd3e25","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-fe042bbacde2/tests/books.rs","newString":"async fn setup_app() -> axum::Router {\n    let pool = make_pool(\"sqlite::memory:?cache=shared\").await.unwrap();\n    // Clear any leftover data from a previous test in the shared cache.\n    sqlx::query(\"DELETE FROM books\")\n        .execute(&pool)\n        .await\n        .unwrap();\n    build_app(pool).await\n}","oldString":"async fn setup_app() -> axum::Router {\n    let pool = make_pool(\"sqlite::memory:\").await.unwrap();\n    build_app(pool).await\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-fe042bbacde2/tests/books.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-fe042bbacde2/tests/books.rs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-fe042bbacde2/tests/books.rs\n@@ -9,9 +9,14 @@\n     String::from_utf8(bytes.to_vec()).unwrap()\n }\n \n async fn setup_app() -> axum::Router {\n-    let pool = make_pool(\"sqlite::memory:\").await.unwrap();\n+    let pool = make_pool(\"sqlite::memory:?cache=shared\").await.unwrap();\n+    // Clear any leftover data from a previous test in the shared cache.\n+    sqlx::query(\"DELETE FROM books\")\n+        .execute(&pool)\n+        .await\n+        .unwrap();\n     build_app(pool).await\n }\n \n #[tokio::test]\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-fe042bbacde2/tests/books.rs","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-fe042bbacde2/tests/books.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-fe042bbacde2/tests/books.rs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-fe042bbacde2/tests/books.rs\n@@ -9,9 +9,14 @@\n     String::from_utf8(bytes.to_vec()).unwrap()\n }\n \n async fn setup_app() -> axum::Router {\n-    let pool = make_pool(\"sqlite::memory:\").await.unwrap();\n+    let pool = make_pool(\"sqlite::memory:?cache=shared\").await.unwrap();\n+    // Clear any leftover data from a previous test in the shared cache.\n+    sqlx::query(\"DELETE FROM books\")\n+        .execute(&pool)\n+        .await\n+        .unwrap();\n     build_app(pool).await\n }\n \n #[tokio::test]\n","additions":6,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"tests/books.rs","time":{"start":1782045841595,"end":1782045841598}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Tests are failing with 404. The `setup_app` creates a fresh memory pool for each call, but the create succeeds (201?) then GET returns 404. Wait actually let me check - the create returned CREATED status? In test, it asserts create_resp status == CREATED. Maybe that's failing too? No, the panic is at line 56 which is the GET assertion (404 vs 200). The create must have succeeded.\n\nWait - if setup_app is called separately and each call creates a new in-memory db, that's per-test, but in `create_and_get_book` the same `app` is used. The create should persist.\n\nActually wait - maybe the INSERT RETURNING in sqlx sqlite returns the row but maybe there's an issue with the GET path. Let me check: each test calls `setup_app().await` which calls `make_pool(\"sqlite::memory:\")`. Each connection in the pool might get a separate in-memory database! Sqlite memory databases are per-connection by default. So the migration runs on one connection, insert on another connection (different db!), get on yet another.\n\nNeed to use a shared in-memory database. Use `sqlite::memory:?cache=shared` or limit pool to 1 connection.\n\nLet me use `?cache=shared` with a shared cache name. Actually for sqlite::memory: with sqlx, you need an in-memory shared connection. The simplest fix is to limit the pool to 1 connection, but then migrations on the same pool work. Actually migrate is called via the pool, so it uses one connection. Then insert uses another from the pool - different db.\n\nUse `sqlite::memory:?cache=shared` - but each unique URI gets its own in-memory db. Actually with cache=shared and same URI, all connections share the same in-memory db. Let me try that.\n\nActually a cleaner approach: set max_connections(1) for in-memory. But that limits concurrency. For tests it's fine. But for production with file db, multi-connection is fine.\n\nLet me just use a file-based temp db for tests, or use cache=shared.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eea358cf9001E1ZK7iTGrbyIP1","sessionID":"ses_115cdbe95ffeGp0717tT7zELj9","messageID":"msg_eea356185001R1aMm2joKkiG1k"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1782045841628,"sessionID":"ses_115cdbe95ffeGp0717tT7zELj9","part":{"id":"prt_eea358a5b001gx5SKd5GYwz345","messageID":"msg_eea356185001R1aMm2joKkiG1k","sessionID":"ses_115cdbe95ffeGp0717tT7zELj9","type":"text","text":"The in-memory SQLite database is per-connection, so different pool connections see different databases. Let me fix the test setup to use a shared in-memory database.","time":{"start":1782045837915,"end":1782045841626}}}
